  "Question": "Marie does three equally time-consuming tasks in a row without taking breaks. She begins the first task at \\(1{:}00\\) PM and finishes the second task at \\(2{:}40\\) PM. When does she finish the third task?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3{:}10\\) PM",
    "B": "\\(3{:}30\\) PM",
    "C": "\\(4{:}00\\) PM",
    "D": "\\(4{:}10\\) PM",
    "E": "\\(4{:}30\\) PM"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "From \\(1{:}00\\) PM to \\(2{:}40\\) PM is \\(1\\) hour \\(40\\) minutes, or \\(100\\) minutes. Because the first two tasks take equal amounts of time and there are no breaks, each task takes\n\\[\n100\\div2=50\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThe third task therefore finishes \\(50\\) minutes after \\(2{:}40\\) PM, at \\(\\boxed{3{:}30\\text{ PM}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
